                                           "verses":  [
                                                          {
                                                              "verse":  "1",
                                                              "text":  "The serpant was more cunning and sly than any other creature in the garden that God had created. They asked the woman ``Is it true that God has forbidden you to eat from any tree in the garden?\u0027\u0027\r"
                                                          },
                                                          {
                                                              "verse":  "2",
                                                              "text":  "The woman said to the serpent: `We are allowed to eat the fruit from the trees in the garden,\r"
                                                          },
                                                          {
                                                              "verse":  "3",
                                                              "text":  "but God has forbidden us from eating or touching the fruit from the tree in the middle of the garden, lest we perish.\u0027\r"
                                                          },
                                                          {
                                                              "verse":  "4",
                                                              "text":  "The serpent told the woman `You will not die.\r"
                                                          },
                                                          {
                                                              "verse":  "5",
                                                              "text":  "God knows that once you consume it your eyes will be opened and you will be like God, knowing the distinction between good and evil, just like a deity.\u0027\r"
                                                          },
                                                          {
                                                              "verse":  "6",
                                                              "text":  "Upon seeing that the fruit from the tree appeared safe to eat, was pleasing to the eye, and would make her wise, the woman took some of its fruit and ate it. She also gave some to Adam, her husband, who also ate it.\r"
                                                          },
                                                          {
                                                              "verse":  "7",
                                                              "text":  "Suddenly, Adam and the woman\u0027s eyes were open, and they realized that they were naked. They rushed to fashion garments out of fig leaves to cover themselves.\r"
                                                          },
                                                          {
