                                                          },
                                                          {
                                                              "verse":  "9",
                                                              "text":  "But God called to Adam and said `Where are you, Adam?\u0027.\r"
                                                          },
                                                          {
                                                              "verse":  "10",
                                                              "text":  "He said `I heard you walking through the garden and I was scared because I am naked.\u0027\r"
                                                          },
                                                          {
                                                              "verse":  "11",
                                                              "text":  "God asked Adam `Who informed you that you were naked? Did you consume the fruit from the tree which I instructed you to avoid?\u0027.\r"
                                                          },
                                                          {
                                                              "verse":  "12",
                                                              "text":  "Adam said `the woman, my companion, she presented me with the fruit from the tree and I consumed it\u0027.\r"
                                                          },
                                                          {
                                                              "verse":  "13",
                                                              "text":  "God then asked the woman `What have you done?\u0027, and she replied `The serpent tricked me and I ate the fruit from the tree.\u0027\r"
                                                          },
                                                          {
                                                              "verse":  "14",
                                                              "text":  "God then turned towards the serpent and said `As punishment for your actions, you are cursed more so than any other animal, and more than any wild creature in the field. You will crawl on your belly and consume dust for the rest of your life.\r"
                                                          },
                                                          {
                                                              "verse":  "15",
                                                              "text":  "Your relationship with the descendants of the woman will be a hostile one. They will crush your head and you will strike at their heels.\u0027\r"
                                                          },
                                                          {
                                                              "verse":  "16",
                                                              "text":  "God then told the woman `The labor pains of your pregnancy will be greatly increased, and you will experience great distress while giving birth. Adam will exert authority over you.\u0027\r"
                                                          },
                                                          {
                                                              "verse":  "17",
                                                              "text":  "And to Adam, God said `Because you obeyed your companion and ate the fruit from the tree which I forbade you from eating, the ground is now cursed and you will have to work hard to gather food.\r"
                                                          },
                                                          {
                                                              "verse":  "18",
                                                              "text":  "The land will produce thorns and thistles, and you will have to eat the vegetation from the fields.\r"
                                                          },
                                                          {
                                                              "verse":  "19",
                                                              "text":  "And after your hard work gathering your food until you die, you shall return to the dust, for that is where you came from. From the dust you came, and to the dust you will return.\u0027\r"
                                                          },
                                                          {
                                                              "verse":  "20",
                                                              "text":  "Twas then that Adam named the woman Eve, The Life Spring, as she was to be the source of life for all living beings.\r"
                                                          },
                                                          {
                                                              "verse":  "21",
                                                              "text":  "God crafted Adam and Eve tunics made from animal hides and clothed them.\r"
                                                          },
                                                          {
                                                              "verse":  "22",
                                                              "text":  "God then said `Look, Adam has become like Us, able to distinguish between good and evil. We must not let them reach out and take fruit from the Tree of Life and eat it, or they will live forever.\u0027\r"
                                                          },
                                                          {
                                                              "verse":  "23",
                                                              "text":  "Consequently, God cast them out of the Garden of Eden to cultivate the soil from which Adam had come from.\r"
                                                          },
                                                          {
                                                              "verse":  "24",
                                                              "text":  "God expelled Adam and Eve and placed Cherubim and a fiery sword at the eastern entrance. The flaming sword moved in all directions to guard the Tree of Life.\r"
                                                          }
                                                      ]
